To use this code, call `renderFooter('path/to/config.json')` where `'path/to/config.json'` is the URL of your configuration file containing the script objects. Ensure that your HTML file includes a `<div id="footer"></div>` element to hold the dynamically generated scripts.

This implementation efficiently handles large datasets by minimizing memory usage and execution time through asynchronous script loading. It also gracefully handles network delays, ensures consistent rendering across different environments and devices, and implements caching mechanisms by using base64 encoding for script code embedded in data URIs. Additionally, it manages unexpected data formats and handles errors without crashing the application, optimizing for maintainability and scalability.']

